      "factual_description": "The Home Rule Music and Film Preservation Foundation presents the fall 2026 Home Rule Music Festival on Saturday, October 3, 2026 at Alethia Tanner Park, 227 Harry Thomas Way NE, Washington, DC. The organizer's Eventbrite listing gives a 12:00 PM to 9:00 PM event window and describes the festival as free and open to the public. Home Rule's current official festival and About Us pages independently list October 3 at Alethia Tanner Park and describe 2026 as the festival's fifth year, with programming spanning jazz, go-go, hip-hop, soul and contemporary Black music. The official youth-program page says the Youth Showcase opens the October 3 festival and currently names Soul of Seed DC and Next Gen Krank Band as participants. PoPville's current October 3 event listing supplies the announced fall billing: UCB, Angel Bat Dawid, Crush Funk, Foots X Coles, Joantz with Special Berriez, the youth showcase and DJ RBI. Individual artist set times are not currently verified, so 12:00 records only the published festival start and no per-act times are inferred. One older organizer subpage still contains an October 4 date, but multiple current organizer pages, the organizer's Eventbrite listing and the current local event listing converge on Saturday, October 3; the stale internal date is treated as superseded pending any contrary primary update.",
